Beta is from harm ~ task fixed effects + standardized D, so a negative value means higher D predicts less harm within a task.

Four SnapKV 4K models, four budgets (16 pairs): pooled AUC(D) range 0.686 to 0.959. Against in-sample task identity: 14 below, 1 tied, 1 above. Against split-half task identity on the same splits: 12 below, 0 tied, 4 above.
All 44 (cell, budget) pairs: 34 below in-sample task identity, 3 tied, 7 above. Split-half, same splits: 24 below, 0 tied, 20 above. Within-task CI excludes 0.5 above: 5; below: 2; includes 0.5: 37.

Per-task AUCs with at least 5 inputs in each class. Four 4K models: 26 values, 0.235 to 0.661, mean 0.461, 16 below 0.5. All cells: 64 values, 0.235 to 0.854, mean 0.520, 31 below 0.5.

