These plain curves have no points between b = 1/2 and full cache, so interpolation uses a long chord and favours the gate. StreamingLLM keeps a constant cache, so its curve is a single chord. These are not reliable matched-cache estimates.

## A4. How -0.69 was selected, and threshold stability (R-Q2, G-W2)

Re-derived fit (relaxed, niah_multivalue excluded): theta_z = -0.6934, cells separated 5/5, balanced accuracy 0.977.
Strict fit (niah_multivalue kept): theta_z = -0.8807, cells separated 5/5, balanced accuracy 0.966.
Thresholds with 5/5 cells separated span [-1.306, -0.587].
Within 0.01 balanced accuracy of the best, they span [-0.953, -0.630].

### A4-T1: Leave-one-cell-out fit

| held-out cell | theta_z | cells separated | balanced acc | held-out cell separated at that theta |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Qwen1.5B-4K | -0.693 | 4/4 | 0.973 | yes |
| Qwen3B-4K | -0.693 | 4/4 | 0.976 | yes |
| Qwen3B-16K | -0.693 | 4/4 | 0.972 | yes |
| Mistral7B-4K | -0.697 | 4/4 | 0.994 | yes |
| Mistral7B-16K | -0.881 | 4/4 | 0.977 | yes |

Bootstrap of the fit (500 resamples of inputs within task within cell): theta_z mean -0.753, SD 0.066, 95% range [-0.888, -0.675], resamples reaching 5/5: 100%.

The fit standardizes over all of each cell's inputs from six tasks, so it uses task labels (in the objective) and a mix that is not a separate pilot.

